## Rows skipped or modified
- a#11 and b#15 (space thousands, unit after the amount): skipped. ACCEPTED and R14 require the dot (“500.000”). A space (“500 000”) fails the checker. Existing TWD amounts left as-is, including “TWD 1.57M”.
- a#13 figure: “1,57 miljonit TWD” skipped (test-pinned, byte-identical “TWD 1.57M”). Surrounding sentence now says the first-instance court awarded it (“esimese astme kohus mõistis välja TWD 1.57M”).
- a#6, b#3, a#35 Gregorian years 2023/2020: not added (R13). ROC framing used. a#35 does not repeat 112年憲判字第4號 (would double-count 112 and 4); the sentence points back to that decision and keeps “seisuga 25. juuli 2026”.
- a#12 and b#14 date case: not the reviewer’s “27. detsembril 2023” / “1. jaanuarist 2024”. The checker’s Estonian month list is nominative only, and the date regex is `(day). (month) (year)`. An adessive or elative month (“detsembril”, “jaanuarist”) drops the month token and the file fails. Case is on the surrounding word, and the nominative date token stays: “jõustus kuupäeval 27. detsember 2023”, “alates kuupäevast 1. jaanuar 2024”, “seisuga 25. juuli 2026”, “5. juuni 2026. aasta”, “ajavahemikus 1. jaanuar 2025 – 31. detsember 2029”. Same digits.
- a#29 “üks järgmistest” and 007 “registreerimine 1 nimele”: digits kept. “üks” / “ühe” are not counted (ü is not a JS word character, so \b does not match). Replacing the digit would drop a 1. “2. astme” → “teise astme” (teise is counted as 2).
- b#12 “kahte aktsionäri”: wrote “vähemalt kaks aktsionäri”. “kahte” is not in the lexicon; “kaks” is counted as 2.
- b#35 “üks hääl” / “üks või kaks”: “1 hääl iga 1 osaniku” and “1 või enama” stay as digits. The no-board sentence is “ainult 1 või kaks juhatajat” (the 2 is the counted word; the 1 stays a digit).
- b#32 and a#32 block merges: not done. Merging one-sentence paragraphs would change the block count. 013’s comma-ended paragraph was closed with a period; the next paragraph starts “Asutamise käigus…”. 015 fragments were made self-standing inside their own blocks.
- Frontmatter url with Hangul (009): skipped (R16). /ko/ link labels only, where a label was already in scope.
- “Kuva kõik”: not changed. The reviewer flagged “Kuva keel” (now “Lehe keel”). “Kuva kõik” is pinned by columns-grid-guidance-labels.test.tsx, which is outside the required vitest paths.
- 015 “Võite tasuta uurida”: left. It is a free lookup of a public register, not a free consultation.
- 002 “jääkvara (剩餘財產)” after liquidation: left. That is residual estate, not the marital claim.
- “lapse parimad huvid” and the employee’s sales record in 008: left. They are a legal standard and a fact, not an advertising superlative.

